hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
1449,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Allah said"
1450,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, They say Al-Karm (the generous)"
1451,Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents
1452,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Not to wish to be the like of except the like of two (persons): a man whom Allah has given the knowledge of the Qur'an and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day; and a man whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it (in Allah's Cause) during the hours of the night and during the hours of the day."""""
1453,"Narrated Sal:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said, \None of you should say Khabuthat Nafsi but he is recommended to say 'Laqisat \nNafsi (See Hadith No. 202)"""
